  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 401 PM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nFor the remainder of the week, as the upper-level ridge continues \nreceding eastward with amplified ridging setting up over the Great \nLakes area and a shortwave ridge centered over the Mississippi River \nValley, the forecast area will remain along the periphery of the \natmospheric flow and see impacts from shortwave disturbances riding \nthat flow. These impacts look to primarily be overnight, with \nTuesday evening/Wednesday morning looking to be the onset of this \n\"ridge rider\" activity (30-50% PoPs). Wednesday evening into \nThursday looks to be much the same, before a deepening upper-level \ntrough digs down from the northern Plains Thursday night into \nFriday. For those who have been following along at home, this \nfeature has been consistent through several forecast cycles. \nHowever, unlike previous cycles, there is greater agreement between \nsynoptic guidance on the placement of this upper-level trough. The \nimplication for our forecast area would be greater confidence in a \nboundary draped through the central CONUS invigorating chances for \nprecipitation (50-70%) Thursday evening into Friday morning. \nAlthough specific details this far out are still not certain enough \nfor a definitive statement on impacts, subsequent forecast cycles \nwill have to monitor trends to evaluate if there is an associated \nsevere/hydro threat with this activity. At present, there is a \nconsistent, strong signal for this system to impact us by the end of \nthe week. After the passage of this trough, upper-level ridging \nlooks to build back in relatively quick, drying out the remainder of \nthe forecast period.",
